From: Emily Astranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: qcom-wdt: arm the watchdog at probe

Start the APSS watchdog as soon as it probes and mark it running, so the
watchdog core pings it until userspace opens the device. A boot that hangs
hard with no console then ends in a watchdog bite and a warm reset instead
of a dark phone, and the ramoops console record survives into the next boot.
Debug aid for the SM8150 bringup; in normal operation the core keeps the
watchdog fed, so the behaviour is unchanged.

---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -285,15 +285,15 @@
 	watchdog_init_timeout(&wdt->wdd, 0, dev);
 
 	/*
-	 * If WDT is already running, call WDT start which
-	 * will stop the WDT, set timeouts as bootloader
-	 * might use different ones and set running bit
-	 * to inform the WDT subsystem to ping the WDT
+	 * Always start the WDT here (the bootloader may have left it running
+	 * with its own timeouts) and set the running bit so the WDT subsystem
+	 * pings it until userspace takes over. An early boot hang then ends in
+	 * a bite and a warm reset that keeps the ramoops console record.
 	 */
-	if (qcom_wdt_is_running(&wdt->wdd)) {
-		qcom_wdt_start(&wdt->wdd);
-		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
-	}
+	if (!qcom_wdt_is_running(&wdt->wdd))
+		dev_info(dev, "arming watchdog at probe (%u s)\n", wdt->wdd.timeout);
+	qcom_wdt_start(&wdt->wdd);
+	set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
 
 	ret = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &wdt->wdd);
 	if (ret)
